{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531557-what-if-the-hermetic-order-had-joined-the-order-of-reason","id":1531557,"title":"What if the Hermetic Order had joined the Order of Reason?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-26T16:24:28-08:00","id":1531557,"title":"What if the Hermetic Order had joined the Order of Reason?","content":"Sorcerer's Crusade actually says that this was an option. What do you think would have happened? How would the Order/Union be today? What about the world? Would the Hermetics have left eventually?<br /> Most importantly could it have happened?<br /> Personally i think the Cabal of pure thought would have left asap. Already they have been burning some daedalans for heresy, i don't think they would tolerate it.<br /> <br /> Craftmasons would probably feel like they are undergoing a hostile takeover. I think they would have the exact same fate, perhaps earlier.<br /> <br /> The high guild actually likes Hermetics, from what i recall, at least to the extend that you can like an enemy.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T10:14:26-08:00","id":1531632,"title":"","content":"*While many Hermetics would find afinity on many OoR practices and beliefs, the OoH as a whole isn't a team player. La Salle had to duel so many mages to have the OoH sit with the Traditions that he died, of Certamen, which it's non lethal (well, admitedly some may cheat and damage the opponent ... and idk if all the duels were Certamen - that <i>was </i>the traditional type of duel. It's still pretty impactfull) ... I think that event talks spades over the &quot;character&quot; of the OoH<br /> <br /> *The OoH at that point isn't interested in &quot;joining&quot; with anyone. Best case scenario, they want the others to join <i>them</i>. Even after being forced kicking and screaming to sit at a table with other Traditons, they see the others as tools and try a takeover. OoR may be more nice looking for some, but I would think they're still mages that need to be educated into a better Paradigm, or deployed as tools<br /> <br /> *The idea that the masses have to be protected and educated, that the OoH has in the modern era wasn't a thing back then. Ancient OoH wouldn't entreat the Crafmason idea of bettering the lot of mortals by giving them the tools of magick. Craftmasons founded the OoR because they wanted to face the OoH, agreed that it would feel like a takeover, it may well be exactly that<br /> <br /> *On the other hand, the more &quot;inquisitorial&quot; aspect of figthing against the supernatural to protect the masses could be approached. OoH do see the role of the mage as wizard-king, and noblesse oblige could mean something. On this end I could see some level of aproach with the Cabal, out of convinience. Albeit giving the cheeky attitude of OoH and how fanatical the Cabal it's, it's going to be a dangerous partnership<br /> <br /> *On Europe they were the major force once uppon a time. The Traditions, thus, would be forced to be much less eurocentrinc. They would be quite the underdogs there. Traditions could become stronger on africa, as maybe the Ngoma would've joined as a full Trad w/o the Hermetics as gatekeepers<br /> <br /> *The Guild will like the Hermetic, as an asset. And I think if they don't leave (likely) or take over (less likely) they may end getting liquidated by them. Nobody likes the OoH as a sort of &quot;fifth column&quot; of wizards that feel superior not just to the masses, but also to the other enligthened. The other factions are going to be feed up with them and join against them eventually - if they don't change.<br /> And the Guild could end causing their downfall because they control the &quot;bottom line&quot;, that's something the ancient OoH really has trouble grasping (they could end having the floor removed in a similar vein as how merchants did the noble)<br /> <br /> Alternatively to takeovers and just leaving, I think the OoH could become the foundation of a stronger NWO. OoH are the masters of symbols, that already had a lot of covert power by creating secret orders attracting people on high places. Once the more &quot;lunatic wizard-king&quot; members have been calmed, the subtler, more politically oriented, parts of the order could take the role of social control and shadow behind the goverment that NWO has. Perhaps less Big Brother and more Illuminati (less transparent but less controling?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-27-2024, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T11:27:05-08:00","id":1531637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531557-what-if-the-hermetic-order-had-joined-the-order-of-reason?p=1531632#post1531632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*While many Hermetics would find afinity on many OoR practices and beliefs, the OoH as a whole isn't a team player. La Salle had to duel so many mages to have the OoH sit with the Traditions that he died, of Certamen, which it's non lethal (well, admitedly some may cheat and damage the opponent ... and idk if all the duels were Certamen - that <i>was </i>the traditional type of duel. It's still pretty impactfull) ... I think that event talks spades over the &quot;character&quot; of the OoH<br /> <br /> *The OoH at that point isn't interested in &quot;joining&quot; with anyone. Best case scenario, they want the others to join <i>them</i>. Even after being forced kicking and screaming to sit at a table with other Traditons, they see the others as tools and try a takeover. OoR may be more nice looking for some, but I would think they're still mages that need to be educated into a better Paradigm, or deployed as tools<br /> <br /> *The idea that the masses have to be protected and educated, that the OoH has in the modern era wasn't a thing back then. Ancient OoH wouldn't entreat the Crafmason idea of bettering the lot of mortals by giving them the tools of magick. Craftmasons founded the OoR because they wanted to face the OoH, agreed that it would feel like a takeover, it may well be exactly that<br /> <br /> *On the other hand, the more &quot;inquisitorial&quot; aspect of figthing against the supernatural to protect the masses could be approached. OoH do see the role of the mage as wizard-king, and noblesse oblige could mean something. On this end I could see some level of aproach with the Cabal, out of convinience. Albeit giving the cheeky attitude of OoH and how fanatical the Cabal it's, it's going to be a dangerous partnership<br /> <br /> *On Europe they were the major force once uppon a time. The Traditions, thus, would be forced to be much less eurocentrinc. They would be quite the underdogs there. Traditions could become stronger on africa, as maybe the Ngoma would've joined as a full Trad w/o the Hermetics as gatekeepers<br /> <br /> *The Guild will like the Hermetic, as an asset. And I think if they don't leave (likely) or take over (less likely) they may end getting liquidated by them. Nobody likes the OoH as a sort of &quot;fifth column&quot; of wizards that feel superior not just to the masses, but also to the other enligthened. The other factions are going to be feed up with them and join against them eventually - if they don't change.<br /> And the Guild could end causing their downfall because they control the &quot;bottom line&quot;, that's something the ancient OoH really has trouble grasping (they could end having the floor removed in a similar vein as how merchants did the noble)<br /> <br /> Alternatively to takeovers and just leaving, I think the OoH could become the foundation of a stronger NWO. OoH are the masters of symbols, that already had a lot of covert power by creating secret orders attracting people on high places. Once the more &quot;lunatic wizard-king&quot; members have been calmed, the subtler, more politically oriented, parts of the order could take the role of social control and shadow behind the goverment that NWO has. Perhaps less Big Brother and more Illuminati (less transparent but less controling?)</div> </div> </div> </div>With regard to the latter scenario, how would the paradigm of the world look like though? In the 15 century, the difference between an enlightened member of the OoR and,say, a member of house verditius can be subtle, due to a very different definition of what science is.<br /> <br /> My opinion is that the Hermetics would end up much more likely to use technological instruments, but conversely, the inner labyrinth ( enlightenment of 4+) might become open tothe outer one. That is, i don't think any artisans would be left with any delusions regarding the fact that they are mages <br /> <br /> I can also see the Order of Reason becoming less &quot;lets improve mundanes lives&quot; and more &quot; lets control the paradigm and fuck everyone else ( that is, more so than it is today)<br /> <br /> The guild would definitely try this approach. I think the order would be quite likely to survive since backstabbing is literally their blood. Plus they would be experience, since they would all but certainly participate in the craftmason purge of the 1670s<br /> <br /> Right, i know they are not interested in joining anyone as &quot;equals&quot; but suppose LaSalle did a score of duels for &quot;Reason and Logic&quot;<br /> <br /> Finally, remember that noblesse oblige begins and ends with protection. The order in my opinion has not changes, its just that the definition of protection has been expanded. (But i can see a renaissance order arguing long and hard that peasants should not know how to write so that can be a huge issue of contention in the later centuries.<br /> In the year 1500, though, i suspect a lot of the more cynical Daedalans might agree, in part as a compromise. The Order was after all, very mighty)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T12:31:57-08:00","id":1531640,"title":"","content":"Well, the &quot;inner circle&quot; especially of the &quot;soft sciences&quot; it's already quite esoteric, with the NWO trying to control history while believing that's not just propaganda, but reather that if you change information the past will change. Or the Syndicate arguing that things like biology (the cure of Cancer) are subject to the free market. To say that one uses symbols and rituals with history behind to focus one's Will to have power over things it's not THAT big of a deal, rigth?<br /> <br /> But yeah the title of Magus and the whole that it implies it's very dear to the OoH, I don't see them ditching those entirelly. Technocrats may rationalize this as &quot;history having power&quot;, which, incidentally, it's true since &quot;historical inertia&quot; it's part of the Foundations IIRC (or even deeper, part of what constitutes them), and I could see the OoH go all &quot;yeah, sure, whatever&quot; about that<br /> <br /> About the &quot;Paradigm o the World&quot;...pretty much anything between &quot;technowizard-punk&quot; to &quot;mostly normal&quot; could be valid depending on how one interprets things.<br /> <br /> From a cosmological pov, I tend to err to &quot;mostly normal&quot;:<br /> <br /> *As I interpret the Mage Setting, science needs to develop with some subtle differences<br /> <br /> I think the Eartly Foundations as we know them favor a world where science develops mostly as we know it. I think mages would have a hard time to make things otherwise. And the pressence of every other Convention suggests - barring a complete takeover - that the OoR will follow a similar path about development<br /> <br /> *It could be - however - a more elitist world, where the education and the &quot;miracles of technology&quot; are even more ill distributed than on our world<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that Jungian psychology could be a good inspiration to make the aesthetics of a blend between &quot;enligthenment rationality&quot; and &quot;occult hermeticism&quot;. I'm not very knowledgeable on the subject, though, it's a very rough idea based on having studied a little about these together","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-27-2024, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T13:13:45-08:00","id":1531642,"title":"","content":"As I recall, of the original Traditions, only the Hermetics and the Solificati knew about consensual reality, and the latter only knew because they were originally part of the OoR. Without the Hermetics the Traditions, if they even form, won't know that vital piece of information until the Solificati defect, if they ever do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T16:48:38-08:00","id":1531709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531557-what-if-the-hermetic-order-had-joined-the-order-of-reason?p=1531642#post1531642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, of the original Traditions, only the Hermetics and the Solificati knew about consensual reality, and the latter only knew because they were originally part of the OoR. Without the Hermetics the Traditions, if they even form, won't know that vital piece of information until the Solificati defect, if they ever do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly talking about the hermetics joining in the 15th rather than the 14 century but good catch. If the order joins the Daedalans, the solificati are like to do as well in my opinion<br /> <br /> I believe the truth about consensual reality was discovered by the order around the yea 1300. Am i wrong&gt;?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T16:50:05-08:00","id":1531710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531557-what-if-the-hermetic-order-had-joined-the-order-of-reason?p=1531640#post1531640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the &quot;inner circle&quot; especially of the &quot;soft sciences&quot; it's already quite esoteric, with the NWO trying to control history while believing that's not just propaganda, but reather that if you change information the past will change. Or the Syndicate arguing that things like biology (the cure of Cancer) are subject to the free market. To say that one uses symbols and rituals with history behind to focus one's Will to have power over things it's not THAT big of a deal, rigth?<br /> <br /> But yeah the title of Magus and the whole that it implies it's very dear to the OoH, I don't see them ditching those entirelly. Technocrats may rationalize this as &quot;history having power&quot;, which, incidentally, it's true since &quot;historical inertia&quot; it's part of the Foundations IIRC (or even deeper, part of what constitutes them), and I could see the OoH go all &quot;yeah, sure, whatever&quot; about that<br /> <br /> About the &quot;Paradigm o the World&quot;...pretty much anything between &quot;technowizard-punk&quot; to &quot;mostly normal&quot; could be valid depending on how one interprets things.<br /> <br /> From a cosmological pov, I tend to err to &quot;mostly normal&quot;:<br /> <br /> *As I interpret the Mage Setting, science needs to develop with some subtle differences<br /> <br /> I think the Eartly Foundations as we know them favor a world where science develops mostly as we know it. I think mages would have a hard time to make things otherwise. And the pressence of every other Convention suggests - barring a complete takeover - that the OoR will follow a similar path about development<br /> <br /> *It could be - however - a more elitist world, where the education and the &quot;miracles of technology&quot; are even more ill distributed than on our world<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that Jungian psychology could be a good inspiration to make the aesthetics of a blend between &quot;enligthenment rationality&quot; and &quot;occult hermeticism&quot;. I'm not very knowledgeable on the subject, though, it's a very rough idea based on having studied a little about these together</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the magitek of exalted is a good example of such a compromise?<br /> <br /> Also what are the foundations? an m20 thing? You mean like cosmological constants, and inertia from previous editions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T19:07:12-08:00","id":1531717,"title":"","content":"Earthly Foundations are introduced in M20, under Reality Zones: they represent a baseline of reality, things that are Vulgar even if the Consensus supports them, and by implication things that are Coincidental even if the Consensus actively disagrees with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T16:04:19-08:00","id":1531755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531557-what-if-the-hermetic-order-had-joined-the-order-of-reason?p=1531717#post1531717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earthly Foundations are introduced in M20, under Reality Zones: they represent a baseline of reality, things that are Vulgar even if the Consensus supports them, and by implication things that are Coincidental even if the Consensus actively disagrees with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, thank you, i think its similar to what Verbena revised had : &quot;Transforming into a mythic beast is vulgar with witnesses, as they have been rejected by the consensus&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T16:48:05-08:00","id":1531760,"title":"","content":"Not quite. If a Magickal Effect goes against Earthly Foundations, it remains Vulgar <i>even if the Consensus accepts it. </i>And vice versa. <br /> <br /> It's similar in some respects to MRev's Cosmological Constants and Historical Inertia, in that they're explanations of why some things' Vulgarity doesn't align with the Consensus. That said: in Victorian Mage, it's stated that if a Territory (Victorian parlance for a Reality Zone) gets completely depopulated and remains that way long enough, it eventually reverts to the Earthly Foundations, with all Consensus-imposed changes fading away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T07:33:35-08:00","id":1531783,"title":"","content":"Earthly Foundations are highly customizable to the type of game you want to run since we have few things that are definitively stated to be foundations, but many things that reasonably could be. They can and do favor the development of science, as they push towards a certain repeatability and reliability. Whether they would always push towards a science we would recognize is less certain, as it's not even clear our world pushes towards a single presentation of science. After all, two theories which both accurately predict the same phenomena and have the same ease of use are equally valid.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T07:31:17-08:00","id":1532026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531557-what-if-the-hermetic-order-had-joined-the-order-of-reason?p=1531710#post1531710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the magitek of exalted is a good example of such a compromise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, especially from an aesthetic PoV. Paradigmatically, &quot;minor-gods and essence powering machinery&quot; it's quite Hermetic, but I don't see it jive much with the other Conventions (that, I imagine, would be at the forefront of technological innovation much like in the current Technocracy) because they seem very materialistic to me, even back. <hr /><br /> Another thing it's that I don't see Hermetics giving up being Mystics (as per the divide between Mystic and Technomancer on Focus). Even if they start using machinery, and adopt a more psychological than metaphisical language, it's ultimately the power of Will what shapes reality for Hermetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T08:47:09-08:00","id":1532034,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that until the 19th Century, the Order of Reason included the Cabal of Pure Thought, which was explicitly religious in nature: \u201cPure Thought\u201d, to them, referred to conformity with the views of the Church. (This started before the Protestant Revolution.) <br /> <br /> I <i>could</i> see something like the Order of Hermes joining the Order of Reason in the early days. Not the <i>actual</i> Order of Hermes, mind you, as the Order of Reason was in many ways a direct reaction <i>against</i> the Order of Hermes; but I could see a faction of Hermetic mages join the Daedaleans, much like the Solificati did. And I could see that resulting in the Order of Reason having more room for mystics in its ranks, as long as they were <i>rational mystics</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T13:23:54-08:00","id":1532185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531557-what-if-the-hermetic-order-had-joined-the-order-of-reason?p=1531637#post1531637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With regard to the latter scenario, how would the paradigm of the world look like though? In the 15 century, the difference between an enlightened member of the OoR and,say, a member of house verditius can be subtle, due to a very different definition of what science is.<br /> <br /> My opinion is that the Hermetics would end up much more likely to use technological instruments, but conversely, the inner labyrinth ( enlightenment of 4+) might become open tothe outer one. That is, i don't think any artisans would be left with any delusions regarding the fact that they are mages<br /> <br /> I can also see the Order of Reason becoming less &quot;lets improve mundanes lives&quot; and more &quot; lets control the paradigm and fuck everyone else ( that is, more so than it is today)<br /> <br /> The guild would definitely try this approach. I think the order would be quite likely to survive since backstabbing is literally their blood. Plus they would be experience, since they would all but certainly participate in the craftmason purge of the 1670s<br /> <br /> Right, i know they are not interested in joining anyone as &quot;equals&quot; but suppose LaSalle did a score of duels for &quot;Reason and Logic&quot;<br /> <br /> Finally, remember that noblesse oblige begins and ends with protection. The order in my opinion has not changes, its just that the definition of protection has been expanded. (But i can see a renaissance order arguing long and hard that peasants should not know how to write so that can be a huge issue of contention in the later centuries.<br /> In the year 1500, though, i suspect a lot of the more cynical Daedalans might agree, in part as a compromise. The Order was after all, very mighty)</div> </div> </div> </div>Gurps has &quot;The Cabal&quot; book about a &quot;Illuminati-esque&quot; group of secret Sorcerors that control the world from the shadows.<br /> <br /> They are exactly what you describe: the Technocracy + OoH, and their modus operandi is exactly that of &quot;screw the masses, control the supernatural&quot;, and they care only about themselves, and their goal is to amass the supernatural in their hands only and deny it for everybody else.<br /> <br /> The Cabalists of the game are just outright villains, unlike the Techies who gravitate between occasional heroes, anti-heroes and villains. The Cabalists of the Gurps game &quot;The Cabal&quot; are just villains upon which not even &quot;for the greater good&quot; matters to them. From a quote from the book &quot;if you had seen what I saw, you wouldn't care about others either&quot;. Whatever good comes from them (as, for example, having a somewhat &quot;safe&quot; world), comes completely as accidental and non intentional byproduct of their actions (they hunt demons and djinns and aliens that defy their power, thus they make a &quot;safer world&quot;, but they don't care at all about the peasants living under their boots).<br /> <br /> There's no redeeming qualities for the Cabal, and this game is a Illuminati game of conspiracies inside conspiracies, and yes, they are much more Illuminati than Big Brother, but the Technocracy at least have a noble goal, even if their methods are tyrannical. The Cabal however are even worse than tyrants. We could say for example that Genghis Khan was a brutal tyrant, but he cared for his nation and for his people's well being. The Cabal would be more like Nero or Caligula, just Narcissists with no limits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T13:31:49-08:00","id":1532187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531557-what-if-the-hermetic-order-had-joined-the-order-of-reason?p=1531640#post1531640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *It could be - however - a more elitist world, where the education and the &quot;miracles of technology&quot; are even more ill distributed than on our world<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that Jungian psychology could be a good inspiration to make the aesthetics of a blend between &quot;enligthenment rationality&quot; and &quot;occult hermeticism&quot;. I'm not very knowledgeable on the subject, though, it's a very rough idea based on having studied a little about these together</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a neat idea. We would have &quot;scientificism&quot; as the new religion and &quot;scientists&quot; as the new priests. And whatever they say become undisputable dogma. And the masses have no saying into it; there would be no YouTube videos about thermodynamics or explaining Calculus, and anyone that graduates at university would simply say &quot;I cannot talk about those subjects to the uneducated. Just accept that A is A because I say it is&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T13:43:36-08:00","id":1532189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531557-what-if-the-hermetic-order-had-joined-the-order-of-reason?p=1532034#post1532034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that until the 19th Century, the Order of Reason included the Cabal of Pure Thought, which was explicitly religious in nature: \u201cPure Thought\u201d, to them, referred to conformity with the views of the Church. (This started before the Protestant Revolution.)<br /> <br /> I <i>could</i> see something like the Order of Hermes joining the Order of Reason in the early days. Not the <i>actual</i> Order of Hermes, mind you, as the Order of Reason was in many ways a direct reaction <i>against</i> the Order of Hermes; but I could see a faction of Hermetic mages join the Daedaleans, much like the Solificati did. And I could see that resulting in the Order of Reason having more room for mystics in its ranks, as long as they were <i>rational mystics</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The real name of the Cabal of the Pure though was <b>&quot;Cabal of the Pure Though OF GOD&quot;</b>.<br /> <br /> They were also called &quot;Gabrielites&quot;, the name by whom they were mostly actually known. And the reason for this name is that allegedly the &quot;Pure Though of God&quot; was delivered to their founder by the Archangel Gabriel himself.<br /> <br /> So yes, they were Christian zealots.<br /> <br /> Also, funny how every single cult irl proclaims to have received a message of God from the hands of Gabriel (like Islam, Mormonism and many others)... That's an interesting detail that the writers introduced here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T14:07:08-08:00","id":1532258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531557-what-if-the-hermetic-order-had-joined-the-order-of-reason?p=1532189#post1532189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also, funny how every single cult irl proclaims to have received a message of God from the hands of Gabriel (like Islam, Mormonism and many others)... That's an interesting detail that the writers introduced here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say you are both overextending the claim by saying &quot;every&quot; and by including Islam and Mormonism as cults. <br /> <br /> Overall, though, it's not terribly surprising. As far as I can tell* there are only two named Angels common to the canon scriptures of Judaism, Christianity, and Islam: Michael and Gabriel. Of those two Gabriel consistently brings messages. He's both the one most likely to deliver messages and the one most thought of as delivering messages. That is to say, I'd expect him to be the most commonly seen Angel in regards to real messages and the most commonly claimed in fake ones.<br /> <br /> *That is, I know the answer for Christianity (it's three named in scripture for the majority of Christians) and I did a quick internet search for Islam and Judaism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}